<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>

	<p>Born and still living in Somerset, England, I'm a father of two and a software engineer who loves music, likes movies and enjoys reading when I find the right book. </p>

	<p>I had started writing a 10 minute-epic tell-all About Me which delved into the darkest depths of my soul, but as I replace that with this placeholding version, I'm not sure if I'm quite ready to be that open just yet. For now I can convince myself that this page just needs to be an "<a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Minimum_viable_product" target="_blank">MVP</a>" to get things up and running... That is what you say when you want to half-arse something.</p>

	<p>Still.... the timeline survived:</p>
	
	<h3>Timeline...</h3>
	<ul>
		<li>1981: Born in Taunton, Somerset, raised in Bridgwater</li>
		<li>1992: First holiday abroad (Corfu)</li>
		<li>1996: Got connected to the Internet and the World Wide Web</li>
		<li>1997: Left school</li>
		<li>1999: Got first proper job that stuck</li>
		<li>2000: Gave up on college</li>
		<li>2002: Went to my first Glastonbury Festival</li>
		<li>2003: Met my future wife</li>
		<li>2005: Moved into first home with future wife. Got first job in tech (front line support)</li>
		<li>2006: Got first job as a developer (Korn Shell (!) working on a Data Warehouse)</li>
		<li>2007: Went to my final full Glastonbury Festival (still hoping to return)</li>
		<li>2008: Moved into kid-ready house, got married</li>
		<li>2009: Had first child (365 days to the day from when we got married)</li>
		<li>2011: Had second and presumably final child</li>
		<li>2015: Joined my current company, which has since merged into others</li>
		<li>2020: Moved into THE house for us (I don't think it is though...)</li>
	</ul>
</BaseLayout>
